Subject: [PATCH] GS uploads: each pixel's address worked out once, in runs
 within a page row

UploadImage wrote every pixel through PixelStorageTraits::Read then Write, which each work out the
address (the page division included). Runs that stay in one row of one page now take the page and
the lookup table's row once and each pixel's address once; the result and the changed test are as
before. A game that streams its textures every frame (145 MB a second in Transformers) had the old
loop as an eighth of the GS thread's time.
---
 ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_cpu_backend.cpp | 9569 +++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 4801 insertions(+), 4768 deletions(-)

